AeneasLoopShim.v
Update_Types.v
Update_FunsExternal.v
Update_Funs.v
Update_Props.v
Update_Safety.v
# Value layer: "ct_eq16/32 returned true" ==> the compared bytes are equal.
Update_Value.v
# P1 — acceptance implies both authentication gates (nonce + tag) were passed,
# over exactly the parsed package fields; plus the nonce gate at byte level.
Update_Auth.v
# The composed security statement: under an explicitly-parameterised HMAC
# idealization, acceptance ==> the tag is the device's own MAC over exactly this
# package's fields, the nonce field is the armed nonce, and (P4) the update slot
# is activated iff its authenticated version strictly exceeds the active one.
Update_Crypto.v
# Conservativity of the mk_array patch at the two extracted arities: an array
# is determined by its underlying list (UIP on Z), so any consistent reading of
# the removed axiom agrees with the total constructors. Nothing imports it.
Update_MkArrayCanonical.v
# Non-vacuity: the extracted parser ACCEPTS one concrete package (vm_compute),
# and rejects it on a flipped nonce / a disagreeing seam.
Update_Reachable.v
# Differential Rust-vs-vm_compute check. Seams (Rocq mirror of the Rust test
# MockHmac; a recorded-tag table seam for the real-HMAC vector) and the
# verdict projection are hand-written; Update_Differential.v is GENERATED by
# `UMBRA_DUMP_DIFFERENTIAL=1 cargo test -p umbra-update-core` and holds one
# theorem per vector: the extracted parser, run by vm_compute on the bytes the
# Rust crate judged, returns the verdict and fields the Rust crate returned.
Update_DifferentialSeams.v
Update_Differential.v
# Mutated corpus (1,000 fixed-seed single-mutation packages, half re-signed
